<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Privacy manifest for the App target.

	Every binary in the bundle declares its own; Xcode aggregates them into the
	privacy report attached to an upload. Capacitor's frameworks ship theirs
	(node_modules/@capacitor/ios/**/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy) and cover the
	UserDefaults access the bridge makes. This file covers the App target only,
	whose Swift is Capacitor's unmodified AppDelegate/SceneDelegate boilerplate.

	All four values are deliberately empty rather than absent, so the file reads
	as an answer rather than as a stub somebody never filled in:

	- NSPrivacyTracking / NSPrivacyTrackingDomains. There is no analytics SDK,
	  no advertising identifier and no third-party network call. The single
	  request the app makes is an HTTPS GET of a public catalogue file.
	- NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes. Nothing leaves the device. Paint lists live
	  in localStorage and are never transmitted. This must stay consistent with
	  the App Privacy answers in store/listing-appstore.md.
	- NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes. The App target itself calls no required-reason
	  API. Add an entry here only if code in this target starts touching one;
	  APIs reached through Capacitor belong in Capacitor's manifest, not ours.

	Note for anyone editing this file: an XML comment cannot contain a double
	hyphen, which is why the notes above are punctuated the way they are.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
